Python Control Flow :
Title: Remove duplicates from list using set

Concept:
Lists in Python can contain duplicate values.
Sets automatically eliminate duplicates since they can store only unique elements.
By converting a list into a set and back into a list, duplicates are removed efficiently.

Tech used :
Language : pyhton
Compiler : Visual Studio Code

Logic Flow:
set(lst_1) removes duplicates.
Converting it back to list(set(lst_1)) gives a clean list with only unique elements.
The order may change, since sets are unordered.	

Input :
lst_1 = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 32, 4, 2, 2, 3, 4, 9, 0]

Output :
Original List: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 32, 4, 2, 2, 3, 4, 9, 0]
List after removing duplicates: [32, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 0, 9]
